[recv] {"method":"item/completed","params":{"item":{"type":"commandExecution","id":"call_m1ACOZq4Wp29fTBtORWxDu1N","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,160p' /root/.agents/skills/tscircuit/elements/led.md && sed -n '1,120p' /root/.agents/skills/tscircuit/elements/resistor.md && sed -n '1,120p' /root/.agents/skills/tscircuit/elements/capacitor.md\"","cwd":"/workspace","processId":"6847","source":"unifiedExecStartup","status":"completed","commandActions":[{"type":"read","command":"sed -n '1,160p' /root/.agents/skills/tscircuit/elements/led.md","name":"led.md","path":"/root/.agents/skills/tscircuit/elements/led.md"},{"type":"read","command":"sed -n '1,120p' /root/.agents/skills/tscircuit/elements/resistor.md","name":"resistor.md","path":"/root/.agents/skills/tscircuit/elements/resistor.md"},{"type":"read","command":"sed -n '1,120p' /root/.agents/skills/tscircuit/elements/capacitor.md","name":"capacitor.md","path":"/root/.agents/skills/tscircuit/elements/capacitor.md"}],"aggregatedOutput":"# `<led />`\n\nLight emitting diodes are diodes that emit light when current passes through them. They are commonly used as indicators on a circuit board such as a \"power on indicator\" or \"data transfer in progress indicator\n\n## Example\n\n```tsx\nexport default () => (\n <board width=\"10mm\" height=\"10mm\">\n  <led name=\"LED1\" footprint=\"0603\" color=\"red\" />\n </board>\n)\n```\n\n## Props\n\nCommonly used: `color`, `wavelength`, `schDisplayValue`, `schOrientation`, `connections`, `laser`, `name`, `footprint`\n\n## References\n\n- Props: [LedProps](https://github.com/tscircuit/props#ledprops-led)\n- Source: [lib/components/led.ts](https://github.com/tscircuit/props/blob/main/lib/components/led.ts)\n- Local docs: [docs/docs/elements/led.mdx](../docs/docs/elements/led.mdx)\n# `<resistor />`\n\nA `<resistor />` is an extremely common element of electronic designs. It limits the flow of electricity and is critical to making sure digital signals are properly \"pulled up\" or \"pulled down\" to set their default value as `1` or `0`\n\n## Example\n\n```tsx\nexport default () => (\n <board width=\"10mm\" height=\"10mm\">\n    <resistor\n      name=\"R1\"\n      footprint=\"0402\"\n      resistance=\"1k\"\n    />\n </board>\n)\n```\n\n## Props\n\nCommonly used: `resistance`, `tolerance`, `pullupFor`, `pullupTo`, `pulldownFor`, `pulldownTo`, `schOrientation`, `schSize`\n\n## References\n\n- Props: [ResistorProps](https://github.com/tscircuit/props#resistorprops-resistor)\n- Source: [lib/components/resistor.ts](https://github.com/tscircuit/props/blob/main/lib/components/resistor.ts)\n- Local docs: [docs/docs/elements/resistor.mdx](../docs/docs/elements/resistor.mdx)\n# `<capacitor />`\n\nA `<capacitor />` stores electrical energy in an electric field. Capacitors are commonly used for filtering, energy storage, and timing circuits. Unlike resistors, capacitors can be polarized (like electrolytic capacitors) or non-polarized (like ceramic capacitors).\n\n## Example\n\n```tsx\nexport default () => (\n <board width=\"10mm\" height=\"10mm\">\n  <capacitor\n    name=\"C2\"\n    footprint=\"axial_p5mm\"\n    capacitance=\"10μF\"\n    polarized\n  /> \n</board>\n)\n```\n\n## Props\n\nCommonly used: `capacitance`, `maxVoltageRating`, `schShowRatings`, `polarized`, `decouplingFor`, `decouplingTo`, `bypassFor`, `bypassTo`\n\n## References\n\n- Props: [CapacitorProps](https://github.com/tscircuit/props#capacitorprops-capacitor)\n- Source: [lib/components/capacitor.ts](https://github.com/tscircuit/props/blob/main/lib/components/capacitor.ts)\n- Local docs: [docs/docs/elements/capacitor.mdx](../docs/docs/elements/capacitor.mdx)\n","exitCode":0,"durationMs":0},"threadId":"019e8ead-3fe9-7073-8d25-1b277e826e16","turnId":"019e8ead-3ff4-7252-8829-239cc99569de","completedAtMs":1780510307424}}
